# BananaOS Master Rule

Building BananaOS: a premium mobile OS in the browser. Every change is production software.

## Non-Negotiables

- No placeholder UI or mock implementations unless explicitly requested.
- Never break existing apps — only add integration points.
- Extend architecture; do not rewrite completed applications.
- `npm run build` and relevant tests must pass before finishing.

## Stack

TypeScript · React · Next.js · Express · MongoDB · Mongoose · Zod · Zustand · TanStack Query · Socket.io

Never use `any`.

## New App Checklist

1. `apps/web/src/apps/<app>/` — manifest, index, store, services, screens, `__tests__/`
2. `apps/api/src/` — models, service, controller, routes; mount in `index.ts`
3. Register: `registerSystemApps.ts`, `storeSeedService.ts`
4. Shared API: `apps/web/src/services/<app>Api.ts` if other apps depend on it
5. Socket events in `packages/shared/src/types/index.ts` + `realtimeService.ts`
6. Docs: `docs/apps/<app>.md`

## Integration Targets

Identity · Banana Bank · Banana SIM · Contacts · Notifications · Permissions · Audit Logs · Realtime · Banana App Store

## Specialized Rules

- UI → `bananaos-ui.mdc`
- Architecture → `bananaos-architecture.mdc`
- Security → `bananaos-security.mdc`
- Animation → `bananaos-animation.mdc`
